    ##         
    ##         If the units given was @link NXOpen::Session::CustomerDefaultSearchOptionNone NXOpen::Session::CustomerDefaultSearchOptionNone@endlink  a second and/or third attempt is made
    ##         with units @link NXOpen::Session::CustomerDefaultSearchOptionEnglish NXOpen::Session::CustomerDefaultSearchOptionEnglish@endlink  then
    ##         @link NXOpen::Session::CustomerDefaultSearchOptionMetric NXOpen::Session::CustomerDefaultSearchOptionMetric@endlink  used instead. The results of
    ##         these attempts can be any of the conditions outlined above.
    ##  
    ##         If you specify either @link NXOpen::Session::CustomerDefaultSearchOptionEnglish NXOpen::Session::CustomerDefaultSearchOptionEnglish@endlink 
    ##         or @link NXOpen::Session::CustomerDefaultSearchOptionMetric NXOpen::Session::CustomerDefaultSearchOptionMetric@endlink  for units, this method
    ##         automatically appends _MU or _EU to the input name. For example, if you  specify 
    ##         @link NXOpen::Session::CustomerDefaultSearchOptionMetric NXOpen::Session::CustomerDefaultSearchOptionMetric@endlink  and input the name 
    ##         "UG_gridSpacingY", the function searches for "UG_gridSpacingY_MU".
    ##  
    ##         If you specify @link NXOpen::Session::CustomerDefaultSearchOptionNone NXOpen::Session::CustomerDefaultSearchOptionNone@endlink  for units,
    ##         the function searches for the name as specified. If the name is not found it searches again with _EU
    ##         appended to the name. If the name is still not found, then it appends _MU to the name for its final search.
    ##         
    ##     
    ##  @return A tuple consisting of (foundCustomerDefault, defaultValue). 
    ##  - foundCustomerDefault is: bool. If customer default was found, returns true .
    ##  - defaultValue is: str. String containing default value. This string will be an empty string if customer was not found. .

    ## 
    ##   <br>  Created in NX2406.0.0  <br> 

    ## License requirements: None.
    ## <param name="defaultName"> (str)  Name of Module ID and default </param>
    ## <param name="customerDefaultSearchOption"> (@link Session.CustomerDefaultSearchOption NXOpen.Session.CustomerDefaultSearchOption@endlink) </param>
    def GetCustomerDefaultValue(defaultName: str, customerDefaultSearchOption: Session.CustomerDefaultSearchOption) -> Tuple[bool, str]:
        """
          @brief retrieves a customer default value from the database.  
        
         
                 There are several different conditions that can arise from 
                querying the database.  First case is the is the record was found and its
                units match. We will return true in this case.  The second case is the record
                was not found. If units given was @link NXOpen::Session::CustomerDefaultSearchOptionEnglish NXOpen::Session::CustomerDefaultSearchOptionEnglish@endlink 
                or  @link NXOpen::Session::CustomerDefaultSearchOptionMetric NXOpen::Session::CustomerDefaultSearchOptionMetric@endlink 
                an empty string is passed back, and will return false. 
                
                If the units given was @link NXOpen::Session::CustomerDefaultSearchOptionNone NXOpen::Session::CustomerDefaultSearchOptionNone@endlink  a second and/or third attempt is made
                with units @link NXOpen::Session::CustomerDefaultSearchOptionEnglish NXOpen::Session::CustomerDefaultSearchOptionEnglish@endlink  then
                @link NXOpen::Session::CustomerDefaultSearchOptionMetric NXOpen::Session::CustomerDefaultSearchOptionMetric@endlink  used instead. The results of
                these attempts can be any of the conditions outlined above.
         
                If you specify either @link NXOpen::Session::CustomerDefaultSearchOptionEnglish NXOpen::Session::CustomerDefaultSearchOptionEnglish@endlink 
                or @link NXOpen::Session::CustomerDefaultSearchOptionMetric NXOpen::Session::CustomerDefaultSearchOptionMetric@endlink  for units, this method
                automatically appends _MU or _EU to the input name. For example, if you  specify 
                @link NXOpen::Session::CustomerDefaultSearchOptionMetric NXOpen::Session::CustomerDefaultSearchOptionMetric@endlink  and input the name 
                "UG_gridSpacingY", the function searches for "UG_gridSpacingY_MU".
         
                If you specify @link NXOpen::Session::CustomerDefaultSearchOptionNone NXOpen::Session::CustomerDefaultSearchOptionNone@endlink  for units,
                the function searches for the name as specified. If the name is not found it searches again with _EU
                appended to the name. If the name is still not found, then it appends _MU to the name for its final search.
                
            
         @return A tuple consisting of (foundCustomerDefault, defaultValue). 
         - foundCustomerDefault is: bool. If customer default was found, returns true .
         - defaultValue is: str. String containing default value. This string will be an empty string if customer was not found. .

        """
        pass
    
